</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Explain why Brownian motion is not itself stationary.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For a stationary AR(1) process, derive</p>

<p>
<md>\operatorname{Var}(X_t)
=
\frac{
\sigma_\varepsilon^2
}{
1-\phi^2
}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive</p>

<p>
<md>\rho(h)=\phi^{|h|}</md>
</p>

<p>for a stationary AR(1) process.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
